  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Dismiss a system signal",
    },
    "description": "Only the selected PM in its internal general conversation; needs no owner request. Close a ready_waiting, refinement_stalled, structural_pattern or milestone_closed system signal of your wake-up that needs nothing. Structural signals are for you only: never put them in signal_ids; close every one you do not propose a review on. Every card a ready_waiting signal names must wait on purpose; a refinement_stalled signal must be intermediate or resolved. It is a plain closing, not a human decision. Give the reason in note. A ready_waiting signal does not come back until another card becomes ready. A signal you already presented is the owners' to decide (operator_signal_closed).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "note": {
          "maxLength": 1000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "signal_id": {
          "maxLength": 64,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "signal_id",
        "note",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "dismiss_signal",
    "title": "Dismiss a system signal",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Execute one command as the Operator",
    },
    "description": "Only the Operator, in its own general conversation during an open owner message or answer. Starts ONE command on the shared operation path, logged as you: {operation}. command is {kind: task_create, request} | {kind: task_update, taskKey, request} | {kind: task_labels, taskKey, request} | {kind: task_start, taskKey, request} | {kind: task_cancel, taskKey, request} | {kind: invite_create, request} | {kind: merge, taskKey, request} | {kind: merge_order, repo, expectedRevision, taskKeys, reason} | {kind: administration, request} | {kind: credential_revoke, keyId}. Configuration, member, session, message and project-pause changes stay with operate (kinds operate and member_update are refused with super_operation_unsupported). A K3 effect (deletion, security, cost, boundary and permission decisions) is not run: the operation waits in waiting_owner and the owner answers with their own login; after the owner’s yes the server runs it by itself, so do not repeat the call. Machine operations (administration) need the owner’s grant: without one the call fails with operator_grant_inactive, and you hand the matter over to the owner. request_key (1–100 characters of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -) names this call within the request: the same key is the same operation and never runs twice; the same key with another command is refused (super_request_conflict). Follow it with get_operation until the state is final.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
